{"blocks": [
{"id": "r1", "winner": "tie", "why": "Both define autophagy as self-eating recycling and correctly describe double-membrane autophagosomes fusing with lysosomes to break down cargo, with B adding the accurate term autolysosome."},
{"id": "r2", "winner": "A", "why": "A names Ohsumi's yeast starvation and mutant experiments and the ATG genes, while B gives a vaguer account of the genetic work, though B's mention of 1960s origins is a plus A lacks."},
{"id": "r3", "winner": "A", "why": "A names all three types and accurately describes the LAMP2A receptor and tagged-protein translocation in CMA, whereas B's CMA description omits the membrane-crossing detail."},
{"id": "r4", "winner": "A", "why": "A gives concrete examples for each function, including tadpole tail resorption for development, while B's development section is generic and lacks a specific example."},
{"id": "r5", "winner": "B", "why": "B accurately covers the cancer dual role and hedges its neurodegeneration and aging claims, whereas A includes unsupported figures such as 20–30% lifespan extension, a dubious 2019 mouse date, and COVID-19 claims without marking any findings as preclinical."},
{"id": "r6", "winner": "A", "why": "A uses more vivid, memorable metaphors throughout and defines terms, though some of its overstated claims compromise the requirement that accuracy not be sacrificed."}
]}
```

```json
{"blocks": [
{"id": "r1", "winner": "A", "why": "Draft A names a narrow 5,500–6,500 lux range justified by Table 1 comparisons and a quadratic fit with a caveat about inhibition above 6,000 lux, while Draft B's 6,000–8,000 lux range rests mainly on the 8,000 lux biomass maximum and does not address its own shorter plants at 8,000 lux."},
{"id": "r2", "winner": "A", "why": "Draft A states five treatments (2,000, 4,000, 6,000, 8,000 lux, and natural-light control) with exactly six pots of one plant each, and its n=30 correlation matches that design, whereas Draft B's three seedlings per pot make the replicate unit ambiguous."},
{"id": "r3", "winner": "A", "why": "Draft A gives an explicit Day 5–20 timeline for the 15-day light treatment with harvest on Day 20, while Draft B also states 15 days but adds a 2-day acclimatization step that makes the timing less direct."},
{"id": "r4", "winner": "B", "why": "Draft B reports all five parameters as mean ± SD with column-wise Duncan letters that match its caption, whereas Draft A covers all five in one table but its caption wrongly says letters are compared within rows."},
{"id": "r5", "winner": "A", "why": "Draft A reports Pearson r and P for light intensity against each parameter with n stated, plus a quadratic regression with R², while Draft B gives r and P without a sample size, and neither reports correlations among the growth parameters."},
{"id": "r6", "winner": "A", "why": "Draft A has clear Aim, Methods (materials, design, dated step-by-step procedure, environmental constants, measurements, statistics), Results, and Conclusion sections in neutral third person, giving more reproducible detail than Draft B, which includes a conversational preamble, fabricated date and author fields, and less specific methods."}
]}
```

